{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "class EmptyListError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised when an empty list is provided to the median function.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message=\"Input list cannot be empty.\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        raise EmptyListError(\"Cannot calculate median of an empty list.\")\n\n    sorted_list = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted_list[n // 2]\n    else:\n        mid1 = sorted_list[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_list[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2"}
